The hierarchy moves in one card, because a base class and its subclasses cannot be half Moo: SICK::Issuer (255 lines), SICK::Issuer::StepCA (311), SICK::Issuer::SelfSigned (280).

Today a subclass lists its constructor arguments in attributes / required_attributes and the base class checks them by hand in new.

Done when:
- the three are Moo classes (extends), the arguments are has declarations;
- the messages a user of the device list sees stay: ca: unknown key <key> for <class> and ca: missing <key>. The default Moo message for a missing argument is not an acceptable replacement, and an unknown key must stay an error;
- from_ca loads its two classes with use at the top: both are known when the file is written, the require inside the method goes;
- file handling goes through Path::Tiny and SICK::Temp; a key is written under umask 077 as before;
- the step command line is unchanged, argument for argument: t/21-issuer-stepca.t reads back what t/bin/fake-step recorded. Read the header of the fake first;
- t/20-issuer-selfsigned.t and t/21-issuer-stepca.t green, skips named.

